Cite JEWEL: Eur.Phys.J. C74 (2014) 2762, arXiv:1311.0048;
JHEP 1303 (2013) 080, arXiv:1212.1599, and applicable feature papers.
The reference source must be supplied separately, with its original notices.
No modified Pythia6 distribution is included or reused as a standalone library.

Positive exponential integral EIX translated from meix.f, credited upstream to
S. Zhang and J. M. Jing, Computation of Special Functions, John Wiley & Sons
(1996), http://jin.ece.illinois.edu. The original attribution is retained here.

Kinematics preserve selected PYANGL/PYROBO/PYP numerical conventions from the
Pythia6 version supplied with JEWEL. Pythia authors: Torbjorn Sjostrand,
Stephen Mrenna and Peter Skands. The hash-verified modified source is supplied
externally and extracted only for the JEWEL reference tests; its upstream
JEWEL-only use restriction and notices remain applicable.

The legacy MPI hard-overlap numerical component translates selected PYMULT
bin-mapping, survival-weight, double-Gaussian normalization and hard-impact
sampling, screened scale-ordering, massless phase-space and common-factor expressions; Pythia authors are credited above.
It is not a complete or official replacement for the Pythia MPI generator.

The legacy MPI channel evaluator translates the ISUB=96 PYSGQC factors and
PYSIGH PDF multiplication order, with Pythia authors credited above.

The legacy gluon-width component translates the KFLA=21 PYWIDT branch, with
Pythia authors credited above. Other resonance branches are not included.
